  "title": "Twelve known RGB fills mapped to the Brother Embroidery thread chart as PE-DESIGN maps them",
  "description": "An SVG of twelve 20 x 20 mm squares with chosen RGB fills (pure red, green, blue, yellow, cyan, magenta, mid grey, tan, blue-grey, pale pink, dark green, orange) imported by PE-DESIGN 11.50 as fill regions; PE-DESIGN picked one Brother Embroidery thread per square: rgb(255, 0, 0) -> 800, rgb(0, 255, 0) -> 513, rgb(0, 0, 255) -> 405, rgb(255, 255, 0) -> 205, rgb(0, 255, 255) -> 019, rgb(255, 0, 255) -> 086, rgb(128, 128, 128) -> 817, rgb(200, 150, 100) -> 348, rgb(50, 100, 150) -> 070, rgb(240, 200, 220) -> 124, rgb(20, 80, 40) -> 415, rgb(255, 128, 0) -> 214. OpenStitch draws the same squares with the same RGB fills; the thread table of its PES is compared with PE-DESIGN's (issue #119: the nearest-thread distance; issue #136: the built-in palette).",
  "covers": {
    "audit": [
      18
    ],
    "featureMatrix": [
